  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'a) Terton Pema Lingpa''s discovery and extraction of numerous treasures helped revive the legends of the eighth-century Guru Rinpoche (Padmasambhava) and his activities in Bhutan. Explain the role played by Terton Pema Lingpa in reviving the activities of Guru Rinpoche, with specific reference to his treasure discoveries and the treasures that serve as the basis for the rituals and religious discourses of the Peling tradition in Bhutan. (10 marks)', 'a) Terton Pema Lingpa (1450-1521) of Bumthang is revered as one of the five great ''terton kings'' (treasure revealers). Guru Rinpoche is believed to have hidden teachings and sacred objects (terma) in Bhutan in the 8th century, to be revealed at the right time. Pema Lingpa discovered many of them - most famously at Mebar Tsho (the Burning Lake) in Tang, Bumthang, where he entered the water holding a burning butter lamp and emerged with a treasure, the lamp still burning. His discoveries of texts, statues and relics proved and revived the stories of Guru Rinpoche''s presence in Bhutan, made places like Bumthang''s sacred sites centres of pilgrimage, and inspired faith in the Nyingma teachings. His revealed treasures form the basis of the Peling tradition: its teachings, empowerments, rituals and the sacred mask dances he composed (performed in many tshechus), and temples such as Tamzhing Lhakhang that he built. The Peling lineage continues through incarnations at Gangteng and other monasteries, and his descendants include the noble families from which the Wangchuck dynasty descends.', null, '[{"point": "Pema Lingpa (1450-1521), Bumthang, one of the five terton kings; discovered treasures (terma) hidden by Guru Rinpoche - Mebar Tsho (Burning Lake) in Tang; texts, statues, relics; revived belief in Guru''s activities and sacred sites", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Peling tradition: teachings, rituals, empowerments, sacred dances (Peling cham, e.g. Pema Lingpa''s mask dances), temples (Tamzhing), lineage of Gangteng and Peling tulkus; descendants include the Wangchuck dynasty", "marks": 6}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-religious-and-political-founders'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
