  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'b) Zhabdrung Ngawang Namgyel is revered as a great religious and political leader who created a unified nation state under theocratic rule in Bhutan - his most enduring legacy. Discuss the contributions of Zhabdrung Ngawang Namgyel as consolidator, unifier and political leader. (10 marks)', 'b) Zhabdrung Ngawang Namgyel came to Bhutan from Ralung in Tibet in 1616.
As consolidator: he established the Drukpa Kagyu school as the dominant tradition, built dzongs - Simtokha (1629), Punakha, Wangdue, Paro, Trongsa and others - that served as both religious and administrative centres, and founded the state monastic body (Dratshang).
As unifier: he overcame rival religious schools and local chieftains, repelled several Tibetan invasions, and brought the scattered valleys of western and central Bhutan under one authority, giving the country the name Druk Yul.
As political leader: he created the dual system of governance (Chhoe-sid nyi), with the Je Khenpo heading religious affairs and the Desi heading civil administration, assisted by Penlops and Dzongpons; codified laws (the Tsa Yig); and shaped a distinct Bhutanese identity through customs, dress, festivals and etiquette. This unified nation state is his most enduring legacy.', null, '[{"point": "Consolidator: arrived 1616, established Drukpa Kagyu supremacy, built dzongs (Simtokha 1629, Punakha, Wangdue, Paro, Trongsa etc.) as administrative-religious centres, monastic body", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Unifier and political leader: defeated Tibetan invasions and rival lamas, unified western/ central valleys into one state ''Druk'', created dual system (Chhoe-sid nyi) with Je Khenpo and Desi, codified laws (Tsa Yig), distinct identity, culture and customs", "marks": 6}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-religious-and-political-founders'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
