  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'a) Of the three institutions of Penlop (Choetse Penlop, Daga Penlop and Paro Penlop) established by Zhabdrung Ngawang Namgyel, the institution of the Choetse Penlop still holds special significance in the political history of Bhutan. Explain the historical background of the Choetse Penlop and its symbolic and functional significance. (10 marks)', 'a) Historical background: Zhabdrung Ngawang Namgyel appointed regional governors (Penlops) to administer the country - the Paro Penlop for the west, the Daga Penlop and the Choetse Penlop, based at Chhoekhor Rabtentse (Trongsa) Dzong, for central and eastern Bhutan. The first Choetse Penlop was Chogyal Minjur Tenpa in the 17th century, who extended Drukpa rule over central and eastern Bhutan. Because Trongsa controlled the main route between east and west, the Choetse Penlop became the most powerful regional ruler.
Significance: in the 19th century, Trongsa Penlop Jigme Namgyel became the dominant power, and his son, Trongsa Penlop Ugyen Wangchuck, unified the country and was enthroned as the first hereditary King in 1907. Since then, the institution has symbolised the royal succession: the Crown Prince is formally invested as Trongsa Penlop (receiving the red scarf) before ascending the Throne - as His Majesty the Fifth King was in 2004. It therefore represents the heir apparent, the continuity of the Wangchuck dynasty and Trongsa''s historic role in unifying Bhutan.', null, '[{"point": "Background: Choetse (Trongsa) Penlop - governor of central and eastern Bhutan based at Chhoekhor Rabtentse (Trongsa) Dzong; first Penlop Chogyal Minjur Tenpa (17th century); controlled the east-west route; most powerful regional post", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Significance: Jigme Namgyel and Ugyen Wangchuck rose as Trongsa Penlops, leading to the monarchy (1907); since then the Crown Prince is invested as Trongsa Penlop before ascending the Throne - symbol of heir apparent and continuity of the dynasty", "marks": 6}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-institutions-and-the-fourth-king'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
