  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'b) His Majesty the Fourth King Jigme Singye Wangchuck''s reign from 1972 to 2006 can aptly be termed ''the Golden Era'' in the history of modern Bhutan. Discuss some of the major accomplishments of His Majesty the Fourth King in terms of good governance and environmental conservation. (10 marks)', 'b) Good governance: His Majesty introduced decentralisation through the Dzongkhag Yargay Tshogchung (1981) and Gewog Yargay Tshogchung (1991), giving people a voice in planning; in 1998 he devolved executive powers to an elected Council of Ministers and introduced a mechanism for a vote of confidence on the King; he initiated the drafting of the Constitution in 2001 and personally explained it to people across the country, leading to parliamentary democracy in 2008; he established the Anti-Corruption Commission (2006) and strengthened the judiciary; and he gave the world the philosophy of Gross National Happiness, guiding balanced development.
Environmental conservation: he ensured the policy of maintaining at least 60% forest cover (later in the Constitution); expanded the network of protected areas and biological corridors covering about half the country; supported the Bhutan Trust Fund for Environmental Conservation (1991), the National Environment Commission and the Forest and Nature Conservation Act (1995); required environmental assessment for development; and put conservation at the heart of development. He received the UNEP Champions of the Earth award (2005) for this leadership.', null, '[{"point": "Good governance: decentralisation (DYT 1981, GYT 1991), devolution of executive power to elected Council of Ministers (1998), Constitution drafting (2001-2008) and transition to democracy, ACC (2006), GNH as development philosophy, judiciary strengthened", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Environment: 60% forest cover policy, protected area network and biological corridors, Bhutan Trust Fund for Environmental Conservation (1991), NEC, Forest and Nature Conservation Act 1995, environmental assessment, plastic ban, UNEP Champions of the Earth (2005)", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-institutions-and-the-fourth-king'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
    1080, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
    '{"verdict": "pass", "issues": [], "checker_notes": "Model answer, marking guide and rubric written by Claude from the RCSC paper; facts were checked against what is widely published, but please read before publishing. Real past-paper questions keep RCSC wording.", "batch": "ME Paper III (General): BCSE 2023, batch 2", "source": {"title": "BCSE 2023 Main Examination, General category, Paper III", "year": 2023, "url": "https://rcsc.gov.bt/bcse-past-question-papers/"}}'::jsonb, 'me-general-3-2023b2-a3', 2, null, null, null, null)
